.TH vix 1  "vix " 
.SH NAME
vix \- Vix: Simple Terminal Rust IDE
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvix\fR [\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-locale\fR] [\fB\-\-diff\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-tutor\fR] [\fB\-\-doctor\fR] [\fB\-\-export\-settings\fR] [\fB\-\-import\-settings\fR] [\fB\-\-mcp\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\-agent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIFILES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Vix: Simple Terminal Rust IDE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-locale\fR \fI<LOCALE>\fR
UI language as a locale code (e.g. en, es, fr, de, cy). Overrides the saved `locale` setting for this run only
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR \fI<OLD>\fR\fI \fR\fI<NEW>\fR
Open a read\-only unified\-diff overlay comparing two files directly, bypassing the active buffer — the shape a `git difftool` driver invokes with (`$LOCAL $REMOTE`). See `docs/cli/index.md` for the git config snippet
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit. Combine with `\-\-json` for a machine\-readable form
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
With `\-\-version`, print `{"name", "version"}` as JSON instead of plain text
.TP
\fB\-\-tutor\fR
Launch straight into the interactive tutorial (also reachable from a running session via **Help → Tutorial**), in place of any files also passed. See `crates/vix\-tutor/spec/index.md`
.TP
\fB\-\-doctor\fR
Check the environment for common setup friction (is `git` on `PATH`, are configured LSP servers spawnable, does the active locale\*(Aqs spellcheck dictionary load, does the terminal look color\-capable) and print a plain pass/fail report, then exit without starting the editor. Also reachable from a running session via **Help → Run Diagnostics**. See `crates/vix\-doctor/spec/index.md`
.TP
\fB\-\-export\-settings\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Bundle `config.toml`, `macros.toml`, `keybindings.toml`, the user dictionary, and the active custom theme into a single file at `PATH`, then exit without starting the editor. Also reachable from a running session via **Vix → Export Settings…**. See `crates/vix\-settings\-bundle/spec/index.md`
.TP
\fB\-\-import\-settings\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Restore a bundle written by `\-\-export\-settings` (or **Vix → Export Settings…**) from `PATH`, then exit without starting the editor — any file about to be overwritten is renamed to `<name>.bak` first. Also reachable from a running session via **Vix → Import Settings…**
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\fR
Serve the Model Context Protocol over stdin/stdout instead of starting the editor, so an AI agent can read this workspace as Vix sees it: open buffers, symbols, outline, offline diagnostics and SQLite schemas. Read\-only. The workspace is the one directory given as an argument, or the current directory. See `spec/mcp\-server`
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\-agent\fR
Serve Vix\*(Aqs remote\-agent protocol over stdin/stdout instead of starting the editor. A Vix on another machine starts this over SSH to work on this machine\*(Aqs files faster; it is not for interactive use. File\-system operations only; exits when its input ends. See `docs/remote\-editing`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILES\fR]
File(s) to open on startup; the last one is focused. A single `\-` reads standard input into an unsaved scratch buffer instead of opening a file (e.g. `git show HEAD:path | vix \-`). A single `ssh://[user@]host[:port]/path` (or `/ssh:host:/path`) works on that folder over SSH (experimental)
